\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Schematic of the symmetric SyN path between two airway trees $I$ (left) and $J$ (right). Top: the two images at initialisation. Middle: after convergence, both images are deformed along $\phi _1$ and $\phi _2$ and meet at the mean shape at $t=0.5$. The full map from $I$ to $J$ is obtained by joining the two half-paths (Eq.~\ref {eq:syn_composition}). Illustrative only; not computed from the study data.}}{11}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:syn_path}{{1}{11}{Schematic of the symmetric SyN path between two airway trees $I$ (left) and $J$ (right). Top: the two images at initialisation. Middle: after convergence, both images are deformed along $\phi _1$ and $\phi _2$ and meet at the mean shape at $t=0.5$. The full map from $I$ to $J$ is obtained by joining the two half-paths (Eq.~\ref {eq:syn_composition}). Illustrative only; not computed from the study data}{figure.1}{}}
